From 9ef4065605b542345e6e45c0264f5a832ff91345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Zhao <yi.zhao@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Feb 2026 20:55:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix mgmtd crash on arm32

Commit 597d79a8 ("lib: improve error handling for datastore
notifications")[1] introduced a retry mechanism in oper_walk_done() via
timer_walk_abort(). On ARM32 platforms, this exposed a potential
alignment issue, causing mgmtd to crash.

This issue is still under investigation upstream[2]. As a workaround,
restore the previous behaviour in oper_walk_done(): on any error, free
the arguments and return immediately, without attempting a retry. This
avoids the alignment trap on ARM32.

[1] https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/commit/597d79a89e6628645e3648bdc03db0d7bdc7e0f4
[2] https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/issues/20087

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Yi Zhao <yi.zhao@windriver.com>
---
 lib/northbound_notif.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/northbound_notif.c b/lib/northbound_notif.c
index 9caca9f6d7..b57ca3382f 100644
--- a/lib/northbound_notif.c
+++ b/lib/northbound_notif.c
@@ -517,8 +517,8 @@ static enum nb_error oper_walk_done(const struct lyd_node *tree, void *arg, enum
 error:
 		__log_err("Error notifying for datastore path: %s: %s", path, nb_err_name(ret));
 
-		timer_walk_abort(args);
-		goto done;
+		XFREE(MTYPE_NB_NOTIF_WALK_ARGS, args);
+		return ret;
 	} else {
 		__dbg("Done with oper-path collection for path: %s", path);
 
-- 
